  "question": {
    "text": "The function $f(x)=a \\sin |x|+b e^{| x \\mid} \\quad$ is differentiable at $x=0$ when"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$3 a+b=0$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$3 a-b=0$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$a+b=0$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$a-b=0$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given, $f(x)=a \\sin |x|+b e^{|x|}$\r\nWe know that $\\sin |x|$ and $e^{|x|}$ is not\r\ndifferentiable at $x=0$.\r\nTherefore, for $f(x)$ to differentiable at $x=0$, we\r\nmust have $a=b=0$.\r\n$\\therefore$\r\n$$\r\na+b=0\r\n$$"
  }
}